  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-MHL126</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved decent work employment opportunities and social protection systems through coherent policies aligned to international standards and labour statistics in the Marshall Islands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO is supporting the development of the Marshall Islands&apos; first National Employment Policy (NEP), a comprehensive framework aligned with the SDGs to promote full, productive employment and decent work for all. The NEP integrates employment into national policymaking and aims to foster a dynamic, inclusive labour market through job creation, skills development, and equitable access to opportunities.

Developed through extensive consultations with government agencies, employers, workers&apos; organizations, and other stakeholders, the finalized NEP reflects broad consensus and commitment. Key focus areas include youth employment, skills enhancement, and job quality. The Government plans to adopt the NEP by mid-2025 and proceed with implementation guided by its action plan.

This initiative is part of the joint programme &#x201c;Accelerating SDG achievement through digital transformation to strengthen community resilience in Micronesia,&#x201d; funded by the Joint SDG Fund. The programme also supports entrepreneurship in the Marshall Islands, including training on the ILO&#x2019;s Start and Improve Your Business (SIYB) Programme. Pilot implementations of SIYB are underway and expected to conclude by June 2025.

Additionally, the ILO is helping improve labour statistics in the Marshall Islands to support evidence-based policymaking. Training has been provided to strengthen local capacity in collecting and analyzing labour market data, in line with international standards.</narrative>
  </description>
